/-!
# Affine chart diagrams with target over the open complement of a Fitting subspace

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S` of a big fppf site, let `G`
be an `𝒪_Y`-module and let `Z ⊆ Y` be the closed subspace cut out by the `k`-th Fitting ideal
sheaf of `G`.  On an affine étale chart `V` of `X` on which the `k`-th Fitting ideal of the
sections of `f^*G` is generated by one function `g`, the basic open of `g` lies over the open
complement `Y ∖ Z`; this file proves that the affine chart diagrams over `f` whose target chart
comes from a chart of `Y ∖ Z` are cofinal over that basic open, with the target chart constrained
by any property `Q` of affine charts holding on a covering of every chart of `Y ∖ Z`.

The cofinality statement of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.generate_affineChartDiagram_mem_topology` (Stacks 03G2) constrains the
target chart only by a property holding on *every* affine chart, so it does not apply; but its
pointwise form does.  A covering sieve of the small étale site is one whose members are jointly
surjective on the points of the chart scheme, in both directions
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smallEtale_sieve_of_pointwise_covering` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.exists_mem_arrows_mem_range`), so it suffices to produce, over
each point of the basic open, one affine chart diagram whose target satisfies `Q`.  That is done
in three steps.

**Some affine chart diagram through the point.**  This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_hasAffineChartDiagram`, the pointwise form of Stacks 03G2 and
Stacks 03H5.  Over its source chart the `k`-th Fitting ideal of `f^*G` is the unit ideal, because
the source chart lies over the basic open of `g` and the chartwise Fitting ideal base changes
along a morphism of affine charts (Stacks 07ZA).

**A function of the `k`-th Fitting ideal of `G` invertible at the image point.**  By Stacks 0CZ4
on one chart diagram the unit ideal upstairs is generated by the image of the chartwise Fitting
ideal of `G` over the target chart, so that ideal cannot be carried into the maximal ideal of the
local ring at the point upstairs: this is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_mem_basicOpen_of_map_appTop_eq_top`, and the basic open of the
function it produces is an affine chart of `Y` on which the Fitting ideal sheaf — hence, by
hypothesis, the defining ideal sheaf of `Z` — is the whole structure sheaf.

**The target chart, moved into the complement and refined.**  A chart of `Y` on which the
defining ideal sheaf of `Z` is the unit ideal has its image in the unit locus of that ideal
sheaf, which is the point set of `Y ∖ Z`; so by Stacks 03IE it factors through `Y ∖ Z`, and
cancellation of an étale morphism exhibits it as the postcomposition of a chart of `Y ∖ Z` *on
the nose*.  The covering hypothesis on `Q` then refines it, pointwise, to a chart satisfying `Q`,
and `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_chart_pullback` carries that refinement back to the source.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.openComplementSpace` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.openComplementHom`: the open complement of a closed subspace as an
  algebraic space, and its inclusion.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.complementChart`: an étale chart of the open complement, read as an
  étale chart of the ambient space.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_mem_basicOpen_of_map_appTop_eq_top`: if the ideal generated by
  the image of an ideal of global functions generates the unit ideal, then through every point of
  the source some member of the ideal is invertible at the image point.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_complementChart_eq`: a chart of `Y` whose image lies in the
  unit locus of the defining ideal sheaf of `Z` is the postcomposition of a chart of `Y ∖ Z`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_hom_of_forall_mem_idealUnitLocus`: such a chart is refined, at
  any of its points, by a chart satisfying a property holding on a covering of every chart of
  `Y ∖ Z`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.generate_complementChartDiagram_mem_topology`: **the cofinality**.

## Implementation notes

**No `@[stacks]` attribute is claimed.**  The cofinality here is Stacks 03G2(4) read relative to
an open subspace of the target, not the tag itself; the tag is registered, in its own shape, at
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.generate_affineChartDiagram_mem_topology`, and a second registration
would be a second spelling of one tag.  Stacks 03IE is likewise already registered, at
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.factorsThrough_openSubspace_iff_points`, and is used here rather than
restated.

The four declarations about the open complement as an algebraic space live here rather than in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/StrictTransformFittingRank.lean`, which imports them: the
cofinality is stated in their vocabulary and that file is downstream of this one.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03G2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03G2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03H5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03H5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03IE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03IE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03LP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03LP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07ZA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07ZA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CZ4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CZ4)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-! ### The open complement of a closed subspace, as an algebraic space -/

/-- The open complement `X ∖ Z` of a closed subspace of an algebraic space over `S`, as an
algebraic space over `S`.  It is an open subspace by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isOpenSubspace_openComplement`. -/
def openComplementSpace (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1) :
    AlgebraicSpaces B S hS :=
  ⟨(openComplement B S hS Z.1).toFunctor,
    (isOpenSubspace_openComplement B S hS X.2 Z.1 Z.2).1⟩

/-- The inclusion `X ∖ Z ⟶ X` of the open complement of a closed subspace. -/
def openComplementHom (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1) :
    openComplementSpace B S hS X Z ⟶ X :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk (openComplement B S hS Z.1).ι

/-- The inclusion of the open complement of a closed subspace is étale after every representable
base change, being an open immersion. -/
theorem presheaf_etale_openComplementHom (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1) :
    (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf (openComplementHom B S hS X Z).hom :=
  presheaf_etale_of_isOpenImmersion B S hS
    (isOpenSubspace_openComplement B S hS X.2 Z.1 Z.2).2

/-- The inclusion of the open complement of a closed subspace is étale: the open complement is
an open subspace, and the inclusion of an open subspace is étale. -/
theorem isEtale_openComplementHom (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1) :
    IsEtale B S hS (openComplementHom B S hS X Z).hom :=
  isEtale_ι_of_isOpenSubspace (isOpenSubspace_openComplement B S hS X.2 Z.1 Z.2)

/-- An étale chart of the open complement, read as an étale chart of the ambient space by
composing its structure morphism with the inclusion. -/
noncomputable abbrev complementChart (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1) :
    SmallEtale B S hS (openComplementSpace B S hS X Z).1 ⥤ SmallEtale B S hS X.1 :=
  smallEtalePostcomp B S hS (openComplementHom B S hS X Z) (isEtale_openComplementHom B S hS X Z)

/-- The point set of the open complement of a closed subspace is the unit locus of its defining
ideal sheaf. -/
theorem range_pointsMap_ι_openComplement_eq_idealUnitLocus (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1) :
    Set.range (pointsMap B S hS (openComplement B S hS Z.1).toFunctor
        (openComplement B S hS Z.1).ι) =
      idealUnitLocus B S hS X (definingIdealSheaf B S hS X Z) := by
  rw [openComplement_eq_openSubspaceOfPoints_idealUnitLocus B S hS X Z]
  exact range_pointsMap_ι_openSubspaceOfPoints B S hS _

/-! ### A function of an ideal invertible at a point -/

/-- **An ideal of global functions generating the unit ideal upstairs has a member invertible at
the image of any given point.**

Were every member of the ideal to vanish at the image point, its image would lie in the maximal
ideal of the local ring at the point upstairs, and so would the unit ideal it generates. -/
theorem exists_mem_basicOpen_of_map_appTop_eq_top {W V : Scheme.{u}} (ψ : W ⟶ V)
    (I : Ideal Γ(V, ⊤)) (hI : Ideal.map ψ.appTop.hom I = ⊤) (w : W) :
    ∃ b ∈ I, ψ.base w ∈ V.basicOpen b := by
  by_contra hcon
  simp only [not_exists, not_and] at hcon
  have hle : Ideal.map ((W.presheaf.germ ⊤ w trivial).hom.comp ψ.appTop.hom) I ≤
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (W.presheaf.stalk w) := by
    rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
    intro b hb
    refine IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal _ |>.2 ?_
    have hwb : w ∉ W.basicOpen (ψ.appTop b) := by
      rw [← Scheme.preimage_basicOpen_top]
      exact hcon b hb
    rw [Scheme.mem_basicOpen_top] at hwb
    exact hwb
  rw [← Ideal.map_map, hI, Ideal.map_top] at hle
  exact (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal (W.presheaf.stalk w)).ne_top (top_le_iff.1 hle)

/-! ### Moving a chart into the open complement -/

/-- **A chart of `X` whose image lies in the unit locus of the defining ideal sheaf of `Z` is the
postcomposition of a chart of `X ∖ Z`, by an equality of charts.**

The unit locus is the point set of the open complement, so Stacks 03IE factors the structure
morphism of the chart through the inclusion; the factorization is étale after every representable
base change by cancellation, `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.presheaf_etale_of_postcomp`, and an object
of the small étale site is a costructured arrow together with a proposition, so the chart built
from it has the given chart's structure morphism *as* its structure morphism. -/
theorem exists_complementChart_eq (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1) (T : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    (hT : ∀ y : points B S hS (yoneda.obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj T)),
      pointsMap B S hS (yoneda.obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj T)) T.1.hom y ∈
        idealUnitLocus B S hS X (definingIdealSheaf B S hS X Z)) :
    ∃ U₀ : SmallEtale B S hS (openComplementSpace B S hS X Z).1,
      (complementChart B S hS X Z).obj U₀ = T := by
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := (factorsThrough_openSubspace_iff_points B S hS X.2
    (AlgebraicGeometry.isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS _)
    (openComplement B S hS Z.1) (isOpenSubspace_openComplement B S hS X.2 Z.1 Z.2)
    T.1.hom).2 (by
      rintro _ ⟨y, rfl⟩
      rw [range_pointsMap_ι_openComplement_eq_idealUnitLocus B S hS X Z]
      exact hT y)
  refine ⟨⟨CostructuredArrow.mk g, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
  · exact presheaf_etale_of_postcomp B S hS
      (presheaf_etale_openComplementHom B S hS X Z) T.property hg
  · exact ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.ext
      (congrArg (fun α : yoneda.obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj T) ⟶ X.1 =>
        (CostructuredArrow.mk α : CostructuredArrow yoneda X.1)) hg)

/-- **A chart of `X` lying over the open complement is refined at each of its points by a chart
satisfying a property which holds on a covering of every chart of `X ∖ Z`.**

The chart is the postcomposition of a chart `U₀` of `X ∖ Z`, with the same underlying scheme, so
the covering hypothesis at `U₀` applies to the given point; a covering sieve of the small étale
site is jointly surjective on the points of the chart scheme, so some member of it contains the
point in its image, and postcomposition carries that member to a morphism of charts of `X`
without changing the underlying scheme morphism. -/
theorem exists_hom_of_forall_mem_idealUnitLocus (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1) (T : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    (hT : ∀ y : points B S hS (yoneda.obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj T)),
      pointsMap B S hS (yoneda.obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj T)) T.1.hom y ∈
        idealUnitLocus B S hS X (definingIdealSheaf B S hS X Z))
    (Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1 → Prop)
    (hQ : ∀ U₀ : SmallEtale B S hS (openComplementSpace B S hS X Z).1,
      Sieve.generate (fun (V₀ : SmallEtale B S hS (openComplementSpace B S hS X Z).1) _ =>
        Q ((complementChart B S hS X Z).obj V₀)) ∈
          SmallEtale.topology B S hS (openComplementSpace B S hS X Z).1 U₀)
    (t : chartScheme T) :
    ∃ (T' : SmallEtale B S hS X.1) (m : T' ⟶ T), Q T' ∧
      ∃ t' : chartScheme T', chartSchemeMap m t' = t := by
  obtain ⟨U₀, hU₀⟩ := exists_complementChart_eq B S hS X Z T hT
  subst hU₀
  obtain ⟨V₀, j, hj, hjt⟩ := SmallEtale.exists_mem_arrows_mem_range B S hS
    (openComplementSpace B S hS X Z).1 (hQ U₀) t
  obtain ⟨V₁, a₁, b₁, hQ₁, hfac⟩ := hj
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := hjt
  refine ⟨(complementChart B S hS X Z).obj V₁, (complementChart B S hS X Z).map b₁, hQ₁,
    chartSchemeMap a₁ v, ?_⟩
  have hcomp : chartSchemeMap ((complementChart B S hS X Z).map b₁)
      (chartSchemeMap a₁ v) = chartSchemeMap (a₁ ≫ b₁) v := rfl
  rw [hcomp, hfac]
  exact hv

/-! ### The cofinality -/

variable {X Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}

/-- **Affine chart diagrams whose target chart comes from the open complement are cofinal over
the basic open of a Fitting generator.**

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of algebraic spaces, let `G` be an `𝒪_Y`-module and let `Z ⊆ Y` be
a closed subspace whose defining ideal sheaf is the `k`-th Fitting ideal sheaf of `G`.  Let `V`
be an affine étale chart of `X` on which the `k`-th Fitting ideal of the sections of `f^*G` is
generated by a single function `g`, and let `Q` be a property of affine étale charts of `Y` which
holds on a covering of every chart of `Y ∖ Z`.  Then the affine étale charts of `X` over the
basic open of `g` which are the source chart of an affine chart diagram over `f` whose target
chart satisfies `Q` generate a covering sieve of that basic open.

This is the chart existence of Stacks 03G2(4), with Stacks 03H5, read relative to an open
subspace of the target, together with the factorization of the basic open through that open
subspace; the three steps are described in the module docstring. -/
theorem generate_complementChartDiagram_mem_topology (f : X ⟶ Y)
    (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS Y.1) (G : Modules.{u, u} B S hS Y.1 Y.2) (k : ℕ)
    (hGcart : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts G)
    (hGfin : ∀ W : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1, IsAffine (chartScheme W) →
      Module.Finite (chartRing B S hS Y.1 Y.2 W) (G.val.obj (op W)))
    (hdiag : IsCartesianOnAffineChartDiagrams B S hS f G)
    (hpbcart : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts ((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G))
    (hZ : definingIdealSheaf B S hS Y Z = fittingIdeal B S hS Y.1 Y.2 G k)
    (V : SmallEtale B S hS X.1) (hVaff : IsAffine (chartScheme V))
    (hfin : Module.Finite (chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 V)
      (((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G).val.obj (op V)))
    (g : chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 V)
    (hfit : @fittingIdealOnChart B S hS X.1 X.2 ((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G) k V hfin =
      Ideal.span {g})
    (Q : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1 → Prop)
    (hQaff : ∀ W : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1, Q W → IsAffine (chartScheme W))
    (hQ : ∀ U₀ : SmallEtale B S hS (openComplementSpace B S hS Y Z).1,
      Sieve.generate (fun (V₀ : SmallEtale B S hS (openComplementSpace B S hS Y Z).1) _ =>
        Q ((complementChart B S hS Y Z).obj V₀)) ∈
          SmallEtale.topology B S hS (openComplementSpace B S hS Y Z).1 U₀) :
    Sieve.generate (fun (U : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
        (_ : U ⟶ openChart B S hS X.1 V ((chartScheme V).basicOpen g)) =>
      ∃ (d : ChartDiagram B S hS X.1 Y.1 f.hom) (_ : d.U = U),
        IsAffine (chartScheme d.U) ∧ IsAffine (chartScheme d.V) ∧ Q d.V) ∈
      SmallEtale.topology B S hS X.1
        (openChart B S hS X.1 V ((chartScheme V).basicOpen g)) := by
  classical
  have := hfin
  -- the `k`-th Fitting ideal of `f^*G` is the unit ideal on the basic open of `g`
  have hVaff' : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj V) :=
    hVaff
  have hVgaff : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj
      (openChart B S hS X.1 V ((chartScheme V).basicOpen g))) :=
    isAffine_chartScheme_openChart_basicOpen B S hS X.1 V hVaff g
  have hfinVg := module_finite_sections_of_bijective_chartBaseChange
    ((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G)
    (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 V ((chartScheme V).basicOpen g))
    (hpbcart V _ hVaff' hVgaff _)
  have htopVg : fittingIdealOnChart B S hS X.1 X.2 ((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G) k
      (openChart B S hS X.1 V ((chartScheme V).basicOpen g)) = ⊤ := by
    rw [fittingIdealOnChart_baseChange_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts
      ((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G) hpbcart k hVaff' hVgaff
      (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 V ((chartScheme V).basicOpen g)), hfit,
      Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]
    exact Ideal.span_singleton_eq_top.mpr
      (isUnit_chartRestrict_openChartInclusion_basicOpen B S hS X.2 V hVaff g)
  -- it is enough to produce one such chart diagram above every point of the basic open
  refine smallEtale_sieve_of_pointwise_covering B S hS X.1 _ _ fun z => ?_
  obtain ⟨W, a, ⟨hWaff, V', q, hq, hV'aff⟩, w, hwz⟩ := exists_hasAffineChartDiagram B S hS f
    (openChart B S hS X.1 V ((chartScheme V).basicOpen g)) z
  have hWaff' : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj W) :=
    hWaff
  have hV'aff' : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS Y.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj V') :=
    hV'aff
  have hfinW := module_finite_sections_of_bijective_chartBaseChange
    ((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G) a (hpbcart _ W hVgaff hWaff' a)
  have htopW : fittingIdealOnChart B S hS X.1 X.2 ((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G) k W = ⊤ := by
    rw [fittingIdealOnChart_baseChange_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts
      ((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G) hpbcart k hVgaff hWaff' a, htopVg, Ideal.map_top]
  -- Stacks 0CZ4 on the chart diagram: the unit ideal is generated by the image downstairs
  have hGfinV' := hGfin V' hV'aff'
  have e := (hdiag ⟨W, V', q, hq.symm⟩ hWaff' hV'aff').some
  have hfinW' := module_finite_sections_modulePullback
    (f := f) (G := G) (d := ⟨W, V', q, hq.symm⟩) e
  have hmap : Ideal.map (chartDiagramRestrict B S hS f ⟨W, V', q, hq.symm⟩)
      (fittingIdealOnChart B S hS Y.1 Y.2 G k V') = ⊤ := by
    rw [← fittingIdealOnChart_modulePullback k e]
    exact htopW
  -- a member of the Fitting ideal downstairs which is invertible at the image point
  obtain ⟨b, hbI, hb⟩ := exists_mem_basicOpen_of_map_appTop_eq_top
    ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map q) _ hmap w
  have hTaff : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS Y.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj
      (openChart B S hS Y.1 V' ((chartScheme V').basicOpen b))) :=
    isAffine_chartScheme_openChart_basicOpen B S hS Y.1 V' hV'aff' b
  have hGfinT := hGfin _ hTaff
  have htopT : fittingIdealOnChart B S hS Y.1 Y.2 G k
      (openChart B S hS Y.1 V' ((chartScheme V').basicOpen b)) = ⊤ := by
    rw [fittingIdealOnChart_baseChange_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts G hGcart k hV'aff' hTaff
      (openChartInclusion B S hS Y.1 V' ((chartScheme V').basicOpen b))]
    exact Ideal.eq_top_of_isUnit_mem _ (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hbI)
      (isUnit_chartRestrict_openChartInclusion_basicOpen B S hS Y.2 V' hV'aff' b)
  -- that chart lies over the open complement, and is refined there by a chart satisfying `Q`
  obtain ⟨T', mq, hQT', t', ht'⟩ := exists_hom_of_forall_mem_idealUnitLocus B S hS Y Z
    (openChart B S hS Y.1 V' ((chartScheme V').basicOpen b))
    (fun y => ⟨openChart B S hS Y.1 V' ((chartScheme V').basicOpen b),
      hZ ▸ fittingIdeal_obj_eq_top_of_fittingIdealOnChart_eq_top G k _ hTaff htopT, y, rfl⟩)
    Q hQ ⟨_, hb⟩
  -- carry the refinement back to the source
  have hwy : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map q) w =
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS Y.1).map
        (mq ≫ openChartInclusion B S hS Y.1 V' ((chartScheme V').basicOpen b)))) t' := by
    rw [Functor.map_comp, Functor.map_comp, Scheme.Hom.comp_apply,
      show ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS Y.1).map mq)) t' =
        chartSchemeMap mq t' from rfl, ht',
      toScheme_map_toOver_map_openChartInclusion B S hS Y.1 V' ((chartScheme V').basicOpen b)]
    rfl
  obtain ⟨W₂, π, p', hp'comm, -, w₂, hw₂, -⟩ := exists_chart_pullback B S hS f W q hq
    (mq ≫ openChartInclusion B S hS Y.1 V' ((chartScheme V').basicOpen b)) w t' hwy
  obtain ⟨W₃, ι₃, hW₃aff, w₃, hw₃⟩ := exists_affine_chart_at B S hS X.1 W₂ w₂
  refine ⟨W₃, ι₃ ≫ π ≫ a, ⟨W₃, 𝟙 _, ι₃ ≫ π ≫ a,
    ⟨⟨W₃, T', (SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).map ι₃ ≫ p', ?_⟩, rfl, hW₃aff,
      hQaff T' hQT', hQT'⟩, Category.id_comp _⟩, w₃, ?_⟩
  · rw [Functor.map_comp, Category.assoc, hp'comm, ← Category.assoc]
    exact (congrArg (fun φ => φ ≫ f.hom) (CostructuredArrow.w ι₃.hom)).symm
  · simp only [Functor.map_comp, Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, hw₃, hw₂, hwz]

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

